OL,3,GNEWSAWhy parts of the West look like
OL,4,Aautumn already
OL,5,
OL,6,FTrees shedding leaves, berries ripening
OL,7,Fweeks early and brown landscapes are
OL,8,Fgiving parts of the West an autumn-like
OL,9,Fappearance despite it still being
OL,10,FAugust.
OL,12,FExperts warn record-breaking
OL,13,Ftemperatures and prolonged dry weather
OL,14,Fare having wide-ranging impacts on
OL,15,Fnature, from wildlife food supplies to
OL,16,Fthe health of the soil beneath our
OL,17,Ffeet.
OL,19,FWildlife conservationist Steve England
OL,20,Fsaid: "Trees should be full of leaf.
OL,21,FInstead, they look how they should in
OL,22,FNovember, but we're only in August."
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,343,340,200,160,0,100
